l  where apple added a silicone pad which  improves grip to the phone  that along with the slightly stronger  magnets means that the apple pack stays  more securely attached to your phone  it's not a massive difference as the  magsafe pack can still easily be twisted  and popped off  but it is an improvement overall apple's  design is sleeker and more simple  there is a single led light that turns  on when something is happening  sometimes when it's not actually even  charging whereas  ankurus has four lights for showing you  the capacity and one more to show you  the status  like if it's on if it's charging or  charging something  and if the device isn't properly working  a huge benefit with apple's pack is the  fact that you don't have to press a  power button first  to make sure that it's on to charge your  phone in fact there is no power button  it just turns on automatically when you  attach it  and it transfers data to your phone  because of this it's also able to show  you how much it's charged in your  battery widget  and if it's actively being charged or  charging your phone  with that the phone can also choose to  stop the charge if it needs to  and unfortunately at this time there is  one use case  where flat out won't charge your phone  and to me  it is really frustrating because that is  one time where i  really want a portable battery pack to  keep my battery topped off  but apple's pack does not do that and  that is  when you are gaming which is one task  which really drains your battery i  started off using a fully charged iphone  12 that had optimized charging turned  off  and my max 8 battery pack was at 50  percent and i played call of duty mobile  for 30 minutes and during that time  my iphone's battery dropped to 90  percent and if you know how iphones work  they show 100 for way longer than other  ones so that is exaggerated  during that time the magsafe battery  pack wasn't used at all  to keep the phone charged which is what  many people say 